# Milestone: M3
# Covers: no strand leak after a block containing '&'-joined strands; Job.jobs
#         count returns to baseline after completion.
# defer-to: M4 (requires Job.jobs introspection and '&' separator runtime)
#
# Reason:
#   The fixture uses Job.jobs.size for strand-count introspection — a M4 stdlib
#   feature.  It also uses '&' inside a block repeated 10 times via 'for' — '&'
#   requires the M5 chk driver.  Job lifetime tracking at the urbiscript level
#   depends on the complete lifecycle machinery including job table management.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M4 with Job introspection and M5 chk driver):
# # var njobs = Job.jobs.size|;
# # { for(var i: 10) {1&2&3}, };
# # assert(njobs == Job.jobs.size);
